<p>What this course is about, how it works, and what counts as your own work</p>

<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128161;</span><div class="callout__content">
<p>Read through this page before doing anything else in the course. It covers what we will study, how each unit is organized, how to look and listen well, and the rules of academic integrity.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="accordion">
<div class="accordion__item">
  <button class="accordion__header" aria-expanded="false" type="button">
    <span class="accordion__number">1</span>
    What This Course Is About
    <span class="accordion__chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9660;</span>
  </button>
  <div class="accordion__content">
    <div class="accordion__body">
<p>The humanities are the fields of study that explore what it means to be human: how people have made sense of their lives, what they have cared about, and how they have expressed it. This course approaches that question through the arts: painting, sculpture, architecture, literature, theater, music, dance, photography, film, and television.</p>
<p>We will not be studying the arts the way an art history course would, as a march of names and dates. We will be asking what the arts <em>reveal</em> about human values, and learning a set of tools for looking at, listening to, and thinking about creative works with real attention. That is more demanding than it sounds, and more rewarding.</p>
<p>The course has thirteen units. The first three build the foundation: what the humanities are, what makes something a work of art, and how a critic describes, interprets, and evaluates. The next ten take one art form each, from painting to television and video art.</p>
<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128161;</span><div class="callout__content">
<p><strong>No experience required.</strong> You do not need any background in the arts to do well here. You need a willingness to look carefully and think honestly about what you see and hear.</p>
</div></div>
