<h3>What to expect</h3>
<p>This is a <strong>self-paced online course</strong>. There are no scheduled meeting times and no fixed deadlines. You move through the material at your own speed, but that freedom comes with responsibility. Plan on several hours of looking, listening, reading, and writing per week, roughly what any three-credit course asks of you.</p>
<p>Work through the units in order. Within each unit the flow is the same: read the Overview, explore the Gallery (or Watch &amp; Listen) and the lesson, try the Experience It activity, write your reflection, then take the quiz. The page <a href="/huma1301/start-here/how-this-course-works/">How This Course Works</a> explains each of these in detail.</p>
<h4>A few habits that will serve you well</h4>
<ul>
<li>Set a regular schedule for yourself; even 30 minutes a day keeps you moving forward</li>
<li>Spend real time with each work before you read what is said about it</li>
<li>Take notes on what you notice, not just what you conclude</li>
<li>Return to a work after you have finished the lesson; you will see more the second time</li>
<li>Try explaining a work to someone who has not seen it; if you cannot, look again</li>
<li>Email your instructor if you have questions or run into problems</li>
</ul>
<h4>Technical skills you'll need</h4>
<ul>
<li>Navigating a website with a browser (you're already doing this)</li>
<li>Playing video and audio in your browser</li>
<li>Creating and saving a document in a word processor such as Microsoft Word or Google Docs</li>
<li>Using a search engine for basic research</li>
</ul>
